From: Francois Guerraz <kubrick@fgv6.net>
Subject: [PATCH] net: ethernet: qualcomm: ppe: fix the Tx NAPI teardown

edma_cfg_tx_napi_delete() disables every NAPI it deletes, the same way
edma_cfg_rx_napi_delete() did, and the second disable of a NAPI spins
forever waiting for NAPI_STATE_SCHED and NAPI_STATE_NPSVC to clear.  The
Tx side reaches it two ways, and both are ordinary:

netif_napi_add_weight() sets those two bits when the NAPI is added and
only napi_enable() clears them.  edma_port_configure() adds the Tx NAPIs
and edma_port_open() enables them, so a port that is registered but
never brought up has NAPIs that were never enabled, and the disable
inside the delete helper hangs on the first call.

edma_port_destroy() deconfigures the port, and so deletes its NAPIs,
before it unregisters the netdevice.  An interface the user has already
brought down has been through edma_port_close(), which disables the Tx
NAPIs, so the disable inside the delete is the second one and spins.  An
interface that is still up is served no better: its NAPIs are deleted
while the netdevice is registered and transmitting, so nothing reaps the
Tx completions until ndo_stop finally runs inside unregister_netdev().

Delete the Tx NAPIs without disabling them, and unregister the
netdevice before tearing down what it is still using.  Unregistering
brings an up interface down first, so edma_port_close() disables the
NAPIs exactly once, and a port that was never up has nothing to
disable.  It also means the Tx rings are disabled and the per-CPU
statistics are freed after the netdevice is gone rather than while it
is still visible.

Signed-off-by: Francois Guerraz <kubrick@fgv6.net>
---
--- a/drivers/net/ethernet/qualcomm/ppe/edma_cfg_tx.c
+++ b/drivers/net/ethernet/qualcomm/ppe/edma_cfg_tx.c
@@ -633,7 +633,6 @@ void edma_cfg_tx_napi_delete(u32 port_id
 		if (!txcmpl_ring->napi_added)
 			continue;
 
-		napi_disable(&txcmpl_ring->napi);
 		netif_napi_del(&txcmpl_ring->napi);
 		txcmpl_ring->napi_added = false;
 	}
--- a/drivers/net/ethernet/qualcomm/ppe/edma_port.c
+++ b/drivers/net/ethernet/qualcomm/ppe/edma_port.c
@@ -351,9 +351,9 @@ void edma_port_destroy(struct ppe_port *
 	int port_id = port->port_id;
 	struct net_device *netdev = edma_ctx->netdev_arr[port_id - 1];
 
+	unregister_netdev(netdev);
 	edma_port_deconfigure(netdev);
 	edma_port_stats_free(netdev);
-	unregister_netdev(netdev);
 	free_netdev(netdev);
 	ppe_port_phylink_destroy(port);
 	edma_ctx->netdev_arr[port_id - 1] = NULL;
